A \times B = \{(a,b) : a \in A, b \in B\}
The Cartesian product of sets \(A\) and \(B\) is the set of ordered pairs \((a,b)\) where \(a \in A\) and \(b \in B\)\(.\)

From notes
A \setminus B = \{ x : x \in A \text{ and } x \notin B \}
The difference of sets \(A\) and \(B\) is the set of \(x\) such that \(x \in A\) and \(x \notin B\).

